<Base title="Credits & sources"><div class="page-shell"><PageHeading title="Made by a community." description="Artwork and writing provenance for this website."/><div class="prose"><h2>Game artwork</h2><p>The homepage background plays a silent loop recorded from the game’s live main-menu colony, without menus or status bars. Its poster is the opening frame. Workers and buildings are drawn by the game itself; no separate unit animations are overlaid.</p><p>{gameplayArtworkCredit}</p><p><a href="https://github.com/Globulation2/glob2">Globulation 2 source repository</a> · <a href="https://github.com/Globulation2/glob2/blob/master/COPYING">Project license</a></p><h2>Logo, fonts and pictures</h2><p>The website shares its look with the online app at app.glob2online.com. The wordmark, the glob icon, the colony scene, and the building, flag and resource pictures are the game’s own artwork (<code>data/gfx</code>, <code>data/highres</code>, <code>data/icons</code>), prepared for the web by the game repository’s <a href="https://github.com/Globulation2/glob2/blob/master/platform/apps/web/art/README.md">web art script</a> and licensed with the game under the GPL 3. Titles use Glob2 Sans, the game’s DejaVu Sans–based font (<a href="/brand/LICENSE-DejaVu.txt">licence</a>); text uses Nunito (SIL Open Font License, <a href="/brand/LICENSE-Nunito.txt">licence</a>).</p><h2>Legacy writing</h2><p>Guide and archive pages link to their original sources. Where reuse rights have not been established, this site provides a source link and an independently written summary rather than republishing the article.</p><a href="/archive/">Explore the archive →</a></div></div></Base>
